+Multijet events can enter the selected sample when a jet is misidentified as a $\tau$ and a jet-energy mismeasurement produces large $\met$.
+A high $\met$ threshold rejects most of these events, but their large production cross section makes additional suppression necessary.
+In the simulated dijet events that survive the kinematic requirements, the apparent missing momentum arises from the mismeasurement of an energetic jet.
+If its momentum is underestimated, the reconstructed momentum imbalance points approximately towards that jet.
+This instrumental contribution is referred to as fake $\met$.
+In signal events, the neutrinos produce genuine missing momentum with no corresponding tendency to align with a jet.
+Figure~\ref{fig:ch7_fake_met} illustrates this difference.
+
